16. Using the API without the browser

The web page is only a client for the /api/process endpoint.

The same operation can be performed directly with curl.

For example:

curl -X POST \
    http://localhost:8000/api/process \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --data @request.json \
    --output pzgis-output.zip

where request.json contains:

{
  "country": "United States",
  "geojson": {
    "type": "FeatureCollection",
    "features": []
  }
}

For a non-US source:

{
  "country": "Japan",
  "geojson": {
    "type": "FeatureCollection",
    "features": []
  }
}

The API response is the ZIP file itself.
17. API endpoint reference
GET /

Returns the PZ GIS web interface.

Use this endpoint in a browser:

http://localhost:8000/

POST /api/process

Processes an area and returns a ZIP containing the generated GIS data.
Request

Content type:

application/json

Body:

{
  "country": "<country>",
  "geojson": <GeoJSON object>
}

Supported country values

United States
Japan
Canada
Mexico
Brazil
Germany
France
United Kingdom
Australia
New Zealand
Other

Successful response

HTTP 200
Content-Type: application/zip

The response contains the generated ZIP.
18. Error responses
HTTP 400 — unsupported country

Example:

Unsupported country: Spain

The supplied country is not in the frontend's current country mapping.
HTTP 400 — invalid GeoJSON

Possible messages:

GeoJSON must be a JSON object.

or:

GeoJSON is missing its 'type' property.

HTTP 500 — processor unavailable

Example:

Could not find pzgis processor: /path/to/pzgis/fetch_gis.py

HTTP 500 — GIS processing failure

The response includes:

{
  "message": "pzgis failed",
  "stdout": "...",
  "stderr": "..."
}

The stderr field is particularly useful for diagnosing the underlying processor failure.
HTTP 500 — no GIS output

If processing completes but produces none of:

buildings.geojson
roads.geojson
water.geojson
landuse.geojson

the request fails with:

pzgis completed but produced no GIS files.

HTTP 504 — timeout

If processing exceeds 15 minutes:

pzgis took longer than 15 minutes and was stopped.

19. Relationship to the downstream map generator

The output of this frontend is GIS data, not a Project Zomboid map mod.

The frontend produces:

area.geojson
buildings.geojson
roads.geojson
water.geojson
landuse.geojson
pzgis.log

inside a ZIP.

The resulting GIS data can then be passed to the downstream Project Zomboid map-generation pipeline.

Conceptually:

                pzgis frontend
                     │
             area GeoJSON
                     │
                     ▼
              fetch_gis.py
                     │
          ┌──────────┴──────────┐
          │                     │
       US GIS              OSM/Overpass
          │                     │
          └──────────┬──────────┘
                     ▼
              GIS GeoJSON
                     │
                     ▼
             pzgis-output.zip
                     │
                     ▼
             PZ map generator
                     │
                     ▼
              Project Zomboid
                  map/mod

The frontend therefore sits upstream of the pz-map-api/PZMapCreation stage described separately.
