21. Minimal operator procedure

For day-to-day use, the entire procedure is:
Start

cd /path/to/pzgis
uvicorn frontend:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

Open

http://localhost:8000

Select

Choose the appropriate country.
Paste

Paste the GeoJSON defining the area to process.
Run

Click:

Process GIS

Wait

Allow the GIS processor to complete. Large areas can take several minutes.
Download

The browser automatically downloads:

pzgis-<country>.zip

Inspect

The ZIP contains the generated GIS layers, the original area GeoJSON, and:

pzgis.log

The log should be retained when troubleshooting or recording a particular GIS generation run.

One detail worth emphasizing from the source: frontend.py does not take the three buildings/roads/area files that the earlier pz-map-api accepts. It takes one area GeoJSON, then fetch_gis.py obtains the buildings/roads/etc. itself.

So the two stages are cleanly:

pzgis/frontend.py → acquire GIS data → ZIP

then

pz-map-api → feed GIS data into PZMapCreation → PZ map ZIP.
